# The annotations of level 8 (11980 bytes loaded at $C4AE by LoadLevel): the source of src/level8/*.asm (kit/mkgame.py).
# The game addresses the level uses are named from src/game/game.ann (@equ). Movers: the entries of the two mover tables
# (LevelMoves, LevelMoves2) MoveEnemies jumps to; each comes back to the game at MoveStore, MoveDraw, MoveDrawA, MoveNext or MoveDone.
@equ $7A82 ScrollStep
@equ $7A83 MetaColumn
@equ $7A84 MapColumn
@equ $7A89 FrameCounter
@equ $7A90 WavePtr 4
@equ $7AA1 ShipColumn
@equ $7AA2 ShipRow
@equ $7AC1 Carriers 8
@equ $7ACD RandomPtr 2
@equ $7DF9 LevelVars 7
@equ $8501 EnemySlots 252
@equ $8CFD DrawSprite 104
@equ $8E85 LevelObject 7
@equ $8EA2 CellMark 32
@equ $9168 MoveStore 6
@equ $916E MoveDraw
@equ $9195 MoveNext 16
@equ $91A5 MoveScript 12
@equ $91B1 MoveDone 43
@equ $C05D NextRandom 13
@equ $C19C BossDestroyed 68
@equ $C20B ClearCells 26
@equ $C225 StartWaveAt 26
@equ $C23F AddScore 31

@module level8data ; Level 8
@about The level's body: the header the game reads at $C4AE, the sprites, the object table, the metatiles, the map, the wave script, the enemy kinds and their movement scripts, the two mover tables and the movers.
$C4AE b L8Header ; The level header: restart point, checkpoints and the pointers the game reads
> Restart column $00, restart wave $0000; checkpoint columns $00, $FF, $FF with wave entries $E6EC, $E8EF, $E8EF; objects $D99C, map $E354, kinds $EBCA, movers $EEAC and $EECC.
$C4AF L8RestartWave ; the wave entry a life restarts at (the game keeps its live copy here)
$C4B1 L8Checks ; three checkpoint columns (CheckRestart)
$C4B4 L8WaveStarts ; the wave entries of the start and the checkpoints
$C4BA L8Pointers ; objects, map, kinds, movers 1, movers 2
$C4C4 b L8Spare ; zeros up to the sprites
$C4E0 b L8Sprites 9 ; The level's sprites: cells of 9 bytes (attribute, 8 pixel bytes) the object table points at
@res levels/level8/sprites.bin
$D99C b L8Objects 4 ; The level's object table: width, height, the cells' address (LevelObject)
@res levels/level8/objects.bin
$DA54 b L8Metatiles 9 ; The metatiles, 144 bytes each (4 x 4 cells of 9 bytes), numbered down from the map: metatile n at $E354 - 144 x (n + 1) (MetatileAddress); 16 of them
@res levels/level8/metatiles.bin
$E354 b L8Map 5 ; The map: 5 bytes a block column (184 columns), each byte a metatile (bits 0-5) and its drawer (bits 6-7)
@res levels/level8/map.bin
$E6EC b L8Waves ; The wave script: entries (scroll position, kind, script) RunWaves starts; then the enemies' movement scripts
@res levels/level8/waves.bin
$EBCA b L8Kinds ; The enemy kinds StartWave reads (LevelKinds)
$EEAC w L8MoversA ; The first mover of each kind (16 words, LevelMoves)
$EECC w L8MoversB ; The second mover of each kind (16 words, LevelMoves2)
$EEEC c L8MoverA0 ; Mover A0
> Witness: L1 0 (none).
